# SakkirinaSolo.cs -> SakkirinaHalf.cs  (search-volume control condition)
#
# WHY THIS IS A PATCH AND NOT A SOURCE FILE
# SakkirinaHalf is 872 lines of code, of which only 36 differ from
# SakkirinaSolo, the 2025 competition winner. Same reasoning as
# scripts/sakkirina_gen.patch: the patch carries only our changes, and
# scripts/fetch_baselines.sh applies it to the author's own file.
#
# SakkirinaSolo is the work of its author and is NOT covered by this
# repository's licence. See README.md, "Third-party agents".
#
# WHAT THIS AGENT IS FOR
# DeepSetsBot evaluates far fewer positions per game than SakkirinaSolo does
# (~102,700 vs ~226,100), because a neural forward pass costs more than a
# hand-written heuristic. That raises an obvious confound: is DeepSetsBot's
# win rate explained by the network, or merely by the two agents searching
# different volumes? SakkirinaHalf isolates it -- it is SakkirinaSolo with its
# per-move time budget scaled by HALF_STRENGTH_FACTOR (0.45) and NOTHING else
# changed, so it reproduces the throughput deficit without also swapping the
# evaluator. It is a control condition, not a candidate agent.
# See experiments/README.md.
#
# WHAT THE PATCH CHANGES (three things, nothing else)
#
#   1. Rename.  class SakkirinaSolo -> class SakkirinaHalf.
#
#   2. HALF_STRENGTH_FACTOR (0.45) applied to the per-move time budget.
#
#   3. The same null-move fix as scripts/sakkirina_gen.patch, so the control
#      and the treatment differ in search volume alone and not in whether they
#      forfeit games to illegal moves. Logs once via BotLog (defined in
#      Bots/src/DeepSetsCore.cs).
#
# APPLY
#   patch -o Bots/src/SakkirinaHalf.cs Bots/src/SakkirinaSolo.cs \
#         < scripts/sakkirina_half.patch
#   (done for you by scripts/fetch_baselines.sh)
#
